window.docContents[78].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.ACD19.Ratchet.LibsignalBound/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___ACD19___Ratchet___LibsignalBound":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session/ACD19/Ratchet › LibsignalBound.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 386 of 552 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (28)def CryptoGames.CKA.MakesAtMostQueriesdef CryptoGames.PRFPRNG.MakesAtMostQueriesabbrev Fig8Advabbrev LCtabbrev FsAdvdef fsSlotCountdef macForgeryTermdef ratchetCostBudgetdef ratchetFsAdapterBudgetdef fsRatchetCostBudgetdef evalTwoStage1abbrev CostedFitsabbrev CostedOpsSizeHonestabbrev CostedSampSizeHonestdef GRedBoundeddef CostedMidFitsdef GTwoStageBoundeddef GRedCostByKinddef GRed2CostByKindstructure FsCostedRedsdef fsCostedBoundsdef pubToADCosteddef multiSlotAdvCosteddef chainPRGTermCosteddef saltPRFTermCosteddef wireOtccaTermCostedstructure Fig8CostedRedsdef fig8CostedBounds\n\nAdversary types, cost budgets and costed reduction bundles for the libsignal session boundTrusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except saltPRFTerm, wireOtccaTerm, multiSlotAdv and pubToAD; the ones they use are part of what you must read to trust the result. Those four are checked by Lean. Refine.SimProg, chainPRGTerm, fsShortBound, fsCompBound, fig8ShortBound and their …With forms are in Computational/Proofs/SpecLemmas/Session/ACD19/Ratchet/LibsignalBound.lean, checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.This file defines the adversary types, the message-blanking map of ACD19 Lemma 18 (Alwen, Coretti, Dodis, ePrint 2018/1037), the per-slot advantage terms of the symmetric-ratchet FS-AEAD bound, the explicit syntactic step-cost budgets, and the ReductionDsl costed reduction bundles used by libsignal_session_sm_r1_proto.Every reduction in the session and E2E bounds is represented as a first-order ReductionDsl.CostedReduction or ReductionDsl.TwoStageCostedReduction over atomicSig ℓ Pt (AtomicOps.lean, TargetCodecs.lean), where every base sort carries an explicit 32-byte block measure sz and multi-step chain iterations, skipped-key scans, and protobuf wire codecs are accounted at primitive granularity. GRedBounded and GTwoStageBounded enforce single-execution step-cost budgets (ratchetCostBudget, fsRatchetCostBudget, ratchetFsAdapterBudget), program size, target query counts, operator/sampler size-honesty, and run-local state and output bounds, while GRedCostByKind and GRed2CostByKind refine step-cost and target-query accounting when game queries are split by kind (online vs. offline random-oracle queries).Because macForgeryProb ≥ 2⁻⁶⁴ (8-byte MAC tag) and each FS-AEAD instance pays 4 * macForgeryTerm C qd = 4 * q * macForgeryProb outside the fsSlotCount qR slot sum (summed across epoch/message guesses and doubled by the window/signed-pre-key authenticity term), the bound is meaningful only for moderately long sessions: the MAC-forgery term reaches 2⁻³² at q = 9459 / 7327 / 1986 / 151 queries for qep = 0 / 1 / 10 / q, and reaches 1 at q = 619925131 / 480191941 / 130210321 / 38967 (see DEV-LS31 in Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md).\n\n\n\ndef CryptoGames.CKA.MakesAtMostQueriesL55–58 ↗#A makes at most q queries to the Fig. 3 CKA oracles (its own coins are unrestricted).\n\ndef CryptoGames.PRFPRNG.MakesAtMostQueriesL60–63 ↗#A makes at most q queries to the PRF-PRNG oracles (its own coins are unrestricted).\n\n\n\nabbrev Fig8AdvL74–76 ↗#Adversary against the Fig. 8 instance lFig8 (messages LibsignalMsgPublicPart × Plain ℓ).\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 78–90): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoGames.LibsignalSM.LibAdv, CryptoGames.LibsignalSM.lBlank\n\n\n\nabbrev LCtL107–108 ↗#Per-message AEAD ciphertext pairing wire (ser, tag) with the 32-byte SPQR salt.\n\nabbrev FsAdvL110–111 ↗#\n\ndef fsSlotCountL113–116 ↗#Active hybrid slot count 2 * qR + (maxForwardJumps + 1) of ACD19 Theorem 5 for a qR-query FS-AEAD adversary: at most qR main-chain slots and qR + maxForwardJumps + 1 lookahead-chain slots bounded by the skip window (DEV-LS10).\n\n4 declarations not shown (lines 118–148): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.pubToAD, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.multiSlotAdv, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.saltPRFTerm, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.wireOtccaTerm\n\ndef macForgeryTermL150–152 ↗#Per-chain MAC-forgery term qd * macForgeryProb C.F over at most qd decryptions (DEV-LS23), charged twice per chain (4 * macForgeryTerm C qd per FS-AEAD instance).\n\n\n\nCosted reduction bundles and budgets\n\ndef ratchetCostBudgetL158–160 ↗#Quadratic syntactic step-cost budget across session-layer reductions (maxForwardJumps = 25000).\n\ndef ratchetFsAdapterBudgetL162–165 ↗#Step-cost budget for the five single-slot and adapter reductions in FsCostedReds that perform no maxForwardJumps-step chain iterations.\n\ndef fsRatchetCostBudgetL167–170 ↗#Step-cost budget for the two-stage FS-AEAD hybrid reductions (prgRedZero, multiRed).\n\ndef evalTwoStage1L172–182 ↗#Sequential evaluation of both stages of a unit-challenge TwoStageCostedReduction at query fuel fuel and default output dflt.\n\nabbrev CostedFitsL184–186 ↗#Recursive block, bit, and list size bound on a ReductionDsl value (ReductionDsl.ValFits).\n\nabbrev CostedOpsSizeHonestL188–191 ↗#Operator size-honesty obligation: each operator o increases the size bound by at most O.cost o.\n\nabbrev CostedSampSizeHonestL193–196 ↗#Sampler size-honesty obligation: each sampler s outputs values bounded by X.sCost s.\n\ndef GRedBoundedL198–224 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, target-query, operator/sampler size-honesty, and run-local output/state block-size bounds for a 1-stage CostedReduction at source query bound q, target query bound qOut, and step-cost budget costBudget. Size bounds are quantified per run via supportWhen (I.AnswerFits B) so interfaces with unbounded Bytes or .nat fields remain satisfiable.\n\ndef CostedMidFitsL226–231 ↗#Block-size bound on a two-stage mid-state.\n\ndef GTwoStageBoundedL233–260 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, target-query, operator/sampler size-honesty, and run-local mid-state and output block-size bounds for a TwoStageCostedReduction at fuel q, target query bound qOut, and step-cost budget costBudget.\n\ndef GRedCostByKindL262–275 ↗#Per-kind step-cost and target-query bound for a 1-stage CostedReduction whose game queries are partitioned by kind : κ → Fin n with per-kind budgets qKind: each query pays only its own kind's handler cost (CostBoundedByKind), and total target queries over (List.ofFn qKind).sum source queries are at most qOut. Paired alongside GRedBounded for size-honesty and run-local value-size bounds.\n\ndef GRed2CostByKindL277–290 ↗#Per-kind step-cost and target-query bound for a TwoStageCostedReduction under query partition kind and budgets qKind, requiring CostBoundedByKind across both stages, zero pre-challenge target queries (init, handlePre, chDone), and at most qOut total target queries. Paired alongside GRed2Bounded for size-honesty and run-local value-size bounds.\n\nstructure FsCostedRedsL292–359 ↗#Costed reduction programs for ACD19 Theorem 5 and the per-message AEAD salt and wire hops on libsignal's symmetric ratchet (fsShortBound).\n\ndef fsCostedBoundsL361–379 ↗#Cost, program-size, query-count, and run-local size bounds for an FsCostedReds bundle at ratchet query bound qR and epoch cap qep.\n\ndef pubToADCostedL381–385 ↗#\n\ndef multiSlotAdvCostedL387–391 ↗#\n\ndef chainPRGTermCostedL393–399 ↗#Slot j chain-PRG advantage evaluated via R.prgRedZero and R.pubRed at query fuel qR.\n\ndef saltPRFTermCostedL401–409 ↗#Slot j salt-PRF advantage evaluated on an FsCostedReds bundle.\n\ndef wireOtccaTermCostedL411–419 ↗#Slot j wire-AEAD OT-CCA advantage evaluated on an FsCostedReds bundle.\n\nstructure Fig8CostedRedsL421–497 ↗#Costed reduction programs for ACD19 Theorem 1, Lemma 18, Theorem 8, and Theorem 12 on the Fig. 8 SM instance (fig8ShortBound).\n\ndef fig8CostedBoundsL499–553 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, query-count, run-local size-honesty, and semantic target-query bounds for a Fig8CostedReds bundle R at SM query bound q and epoch cap qep.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/ACD19/Ratchet/LibsignalBound.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.ACD19.Ratchet.LibsignalBound/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___ACD19___Ratchet___LibsignalBound"}});